 story arc under the marvel  knights imprint and so while kevin smith  only wrote one eight issue arc of  daredevil the story arc guardian devil  remains a fan favorite and in this arc  which is an incredibly dark tone in a  lot of ways is a return to frank miller  this explored matt murdock's complicated  relationship with his catholic faith as  daredevil was forced to take care of an  infant that could either be a new  messiah or the antichrist now of course  kevin smith's story also sees the death  of karen page at the hands of bullseye  but this basically led us into the early  2000s when daredevils enjoyed some of  the most consistent good writing of any  marvel title with several critically  acclaimed runs on the character starting  with brian michael bendis taking over  the title with issue number 16 in 2001  and continuing until issue number 81 in  2006. now venice's run is still seen as  one of the best on daredevil due in  large part to the art of dave mack and  alex malev and an intensification of the  rivalry with kingpin which ultimately  sees daredevil's secret identity exposed  to the world but bendis's successor eric  brubaker stayed on the title until 2009  and his run was also a hit with critics  and fans alike now in 2012 writer mark  wade and artist chris samny took over  the title but by this time because  comics were consistently undoing things  that had basically been done daredevil's  identity is secret once again and he's  basically regained his law license  however by the end of the run he's  basically forced to reveal himself as  matt murdock yet again which basically  results in the state of new york  disbarring him which prompts matt  murdock to move across the country to  san diego now one of the things that i  want to specify here is that the reason  why things were being changed between  2010 and 2011 is because what you had in  this 10-year window between 2000 and  2010 is you had what was called the joe  casada era which has basical